   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **25 ] Red Daisy**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **16 ] I'll Remember You, Love, In My Prayers**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **12 ] Doin' Things Right**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **45 ] Hellbender**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **55 ] The Tall Tall Grass**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **54 ] Taking Water**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **45 ] End Of The Rainbow**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **40 ] Ice Bridges**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2022-08-14.6chAUDmtx_hermsen.mrachek_flac2448** (recommended): source not stated; 23 songs; 128 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **billystrings2022-08-14.6chAUDmtx_hermsen.mrachek_flac1644**: source not stated; 23 songs; 128 min [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2022-08-14.6chAUDmtx_hermsen.mrachek_flac2448**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: DPA 4022 + AKG C568EB + AKG 483 > Sound Devices Mixpre6 [1]. Also: Six-channel audience recording blending DPA 4022 cardioids (about 42%), AKG 568 shotguns (about 33%) and AKG 483 hypers (about 25%); Mics sat on a stand 10-11 feet high, dead center directly behind the FOH console; John Hermsen recorded it; All sources went to an SD MixPre-6 at 24-bit/48; Chris Mrachek, Leftover Salmon's archivist, did the mastering and cover [1]\n- **billystrings2022-08-14.6chAUDmtx_hermsen.mrachek_flac1644**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: DPA 4022 + AKG C568EB + AKG 483 > Sound Devices Mixpre6 [2]. Also: Six-channel audience recording from DPA 4022, AKG 568 and AKG 483 mics, all captured on an SD MixPre-6; This is the 16-bit/44.1 kHz version for CD burning and streaming, converted with dBpoweramp; Mics stood 10-11 feet up, dead center behind the FOH console; John Hermsen recorded it [2]",
